exports[`skills and command templates > two skills, open-format front matter, one source each 1`] = `
"---
name: mandate
description: "Mandate working agreement. Use for EVERY feature request, change, bug fix or work order in a repository connected to Mandate: record the request as feedback, match it to specs, get approval if on, update specs, standards (with user confirmation) and components, create work orders, then implement, verify and reconcile."
metadata:
  managed-by: mandate
---

<!-- managed by mandate: \`mandate uninstall\` removes it; \`mandate install\` refreshes it. -->

# Mandate

Mandate (MCP server \`mandate-<project>\`) holds this project's specs, standards, components, work orders and feedback.
Every feature request, change, bug fix or work order in a repository connected to Mandate follows its working agreement.

**First, every task:** load the current working agreement from Mandate and follow it. It replaces any earlier copy,
including notes in your memory:

\`instructions_get {"name":"core","stubVersion":1}\`

If that tool is missing or the Mandate server cannot be reached: stop and tell the user that Mandate is unreachable. Do not work from memory or from an older copy of these instructions.

<!-- mandate-stub v1 -->
"
`;

